# NextPitchAI — always-on rules

The full project context lives in `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. Read it
before making changes; treat it as the source of truth over anything
inferred from a single file. The run-by-run history is in
`docs/EXPERIMENTS.md`.

Non-negotiables (details and reasoning in `AGENTS.md`):

- Historical features are expanding priors that EXCLUDE the current row.
- Chronological sort (`game_date, game_pk, at_bat_number, pitch_number`)
  precedes every prior and sequence computation.
- Pitch sequences are the same pitcher's previous pitches in the game.
- The arsenal mask is a model input applied to logits before softmax.
- Split train/val before any resampling; report on the natural split.
- One change per training run; append the result to `docs/EXPERIMENTS.md`.
- Never commit `.venv/`, `data_v5/`, `*.parquet`, `*.keras`, `*.npy`, `*.pkl`.

Before proposing a tuning change, check the "Do not retry" section of
`docs/EXPERIMENTS.md`.
